Task: Fix the removeAmazonPeriod function in App.tsx to properly engage the sync lock and prevent the data from "ghosting" back.

The Fix:

Activate the Lock: Inside removeAmazonPeriod, you must set isUpdatingRef.current = true; at the very beginning of the function.

Extended Lock Time: Use a setTimeout in the finally block to keep isUpdatingRef.current set to true for 3000ms after the cloud update finishes. This gives the Firebase listener enough time to receive the "empty" update from the server.

Use Functional State Update: To ensure accuracy, use the functional form of set state: setAmazonRecords(prev => prev.filter(...)).

Copy/Paste this Logic for the Function:

TypeScript
const removeAmazonPeriod = async (periodKey: string) => {
  if (!user) return;
  if (!window.confirm(`Permanently remove all data for ${periodKey}?`)) return;

  // 1. ENGAGE LOCKS
  isUpdatingRef.current = true;
  setIsSyncing(true);

  try {
    // 2. FILTER DATA
    const updatedRecords = amazonRecords.filter(r => {
      const d = new Date(r.date);
      const pk = `${d.toLocaleString('default', { month: 'short' })}${String(d.getFullYear()).slice(-2)}`;
      return pk !== periodKey;
    });

    // 3. UPDATE LOCAL STATE & STORAGE
    setAmazonRecords(updatedRecords);
    const currentLocal = localStorage.getItem(`vista_data_${user.uid}`);
    let packet = currentLocal ? JSON.parse(currentLocal) : {};
    packet.amazonRecords = updatedRecords;
    localStorage.setItem(`vista_data_${user.uid}`, safeStringify(packet));

    // 4. COMMIT TO CLOUD
    const userDocRef = doc(db, 'users', user.uid);
    await setDoc(userDocRef, { amazonRecords: updatedRecords }, { merge: true });

  } catch (err) {
    console.error("Cloud delete failed:", err);
  } finally {
    // 5. RELEASE LOCK AFTER DELAY (The most important part)
    setTimeout(() => {
      isUpdatingRef.current = false;
      setIsSyncing(false);
    }, 3000); 
  }
};

