Task: Refactor the getStandardKey helper function in App.tsx and AmazonAnalysis.tsx (and any other files using it) to prevent timezone shifting.

The Problem: Currently, new Date("Jan 31, 2026 11:46 PM PST") converts to Feb 1st on the user's local machine (MST). This puts the transaction in the wrong month.

The Solution: We must switch from object-based date parsing to String Regex Parsing. We will simply extract the Month and Year substrings directly from the raw text, ignoring the time component entirely.

Requirements:

Replace getStandardKey Logic:

Do NOT use new Date(dateStr).

Use Regex: Capture the first text part (Month) and the 4-digit number (Year).

Pattern: Look for the standard Amazon format: "Jan 31, 2026...".

Regex Example: /^"?([a-zA-Z]+)\s+\d{1,2},\s+(\d{4})/ (Handle potential quotes).

Return: Combined Month + 2-Digit Year (e.g., "Jan26").

Fallback: If regex fails, assume "INVALID" or try the old method as a backup.

Implementation Details:

Update the function in App.tsx (outside the component).

Update the function in AmazonAnalysis.tsx (outside the component).

Update the function in CogsManager.tsx (if present inside processTransactionReport).

